    "body": "## Problem\n\nLSP folding ranges are evaluated as soon as a server response arrives. During\nInsert, Replace, or Select mode, and while navigating a snippet, this replaces\nthe visible fold snapshot while text is still changing. Any fold recomputation\nduring that interval can then close the region being edited.\n\nDeferring only `foldUpdate()` is insufficient because `evaluate()` has already\nchanged the values returned by `vim.lsp.foldexpr()`. When a deferred snapshot is\neventually applied, it can also place a previously visible window cursor inside\na closed fold.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe behavior was reproduced on Neovim `master` at\n[`ca992e82d4`](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/ca992e82d40cb8ed31331ba75cf0a58c6d693ac7),\nafter the nested folding boundary fix from #41428 was merged.\n\nConfigure LSP folding with:\n\n```vim\nset foldmethod=expr\nset foldexpr=v:lua.vim.lsp.foldexpr()\nset foldlevel=0\n```\n\nWhile editing a multiline region in Insert, Replace, or Select mode, have the\nserver return a folding range containing the cursor. The same behavior is\nvisible when a completion expands to a multiline snippet and the user moves\nbetween its placeholders.\n\nBefore this patch, the new fold expression is visible immediately and a redraw\nor mode transition can close the region being edited. After editing ends, the\nnew snapshot can also hide the cursor. With this patch, the previous snapshot\nremains active until editing settles, and a cursor that was visible before the\ndeferred update remains visible afterwards.\n\nThe functional tests use a controlled folding-range server and cover all\nediting modes, snippet transitions, delayed responses, multiple windows,\nexplicit `vim.lsp.foldclose()`, and client detach.\n\n## Solution\n\nKeep accepted folding ranges pending while the current buffer is being edited\nor has an active snippet. Coalesce multiple responses and apply only the latest\nsnapshot after mode transitions settle.\n\nBefore applying a deferred snapshot, record which window cursors are visible.\nAfter recomputing folds, open only folds that newly hide those cursors. Existing\nclosed folds, including sibling folds and folds that already contained a\ncursor, remain unchanged.\n\nExplicit fold-close requests and client detach apply or clear pending state\nsynchronously so they cannot operate on stale fold indexes.\n\n## Testing\n\n```sh\nmake functionaltest TEST_FILE=test/functional/plugin/lsp/folding_range_spec.lua\n```\n\n## AI disclosure\n\nAI tools assisted with analyzing the behavior and preparing the implementation\nand tests. The commit includes the generic `AI-assisted` token.\n",
